/-! # Structured-to-Unstructured Transformation Correctness

This module contains the generic Imperative semantic and trace correctness
proofs for `stmtsToCFG`. The Core bridge and canonical Core gate parameters live
in `StructuredToUnstructuredCoreCorrect`.

Key results:
  * Lowering invariants — `StmtsToBlocksInv` (generated labels are fresh and
    distinct) and `stmtsToCFG_stmtsToBlocks_spec`, which relates the CFG to the
    blocks emitted by `stmtsToBlocks`.
  * Variable and type preservation — `StructuredToUnstructuredWF.Block.cfgLive`
    is the part of the source the CFG keeps; `Block.cfgLive_defUseWellFormed`,
    `Block.mem_initVars_of_cfgLive`, `Block.mem_initTypes_of_cfgLive`, and
    `stmtsToCFG_definedVars_iff` / `_modifiedVars_iff` / `_readVars_iff` /
    `_initTypes_iff` relate the CFG's variables and types to it.
  * Gate transport — `StructuredToUnstructured.cfgInitEnvWF`: a block-well-formed
    source environment is CFG-well-formed for the lowered CFG.
  * Trace simulation — `StructuredToUnstructured.overapproximatesTraces`: every
    finite source trace is matched by a CFG trace under `Trace.WithWF` matching, and
    terminal and exiting environments are related by `EnvStoreAgree`. -/

